    "summary": "Cumberland ’82 delivers soaring Morning Dew and a fiery Spanish Jam > Other One",
    "review": "The September‑17, 1982 night at the Cumberland County Civic Center captures the Dead in full‑tilt early‑‘80s form. The set opens with a rock‑driven Bertha → Promised Land segue that sets a bright tone, but it’s the second set that really shines: Touch of Grey makes its debut, then rolls straight into a blistering Spanish Jam that morphs into an expansive Other One before launching into a soaring Goin’ Down The Road Feeling Bad → Morning Dew climax. Across the board the band rides a high‑energy current – Jerry’s lead guitar is luminous on Dew and GDTRFB, Phil’s bass drops “bombs” that lift the whole room, and Brent’s piano adds that unmistakable 1982 country‑western flavor even when his mic was missing.\n\nWhile most recordings capture the show with crisp clarity, the Harrison soundboard (gd1982-09-17.sbd.harrison.80770.sbeok.flac16) stands out for its rich ambient mix and solid low end, letting every nuance of the jams breathe. Whether you’re after the tight first‑set rock punches or the space‑filled second‑set explorations, this night offers a balanced, inspiring snapshot of the band in a playful yet focused mood – perfect for anyone who loves that sweet spot between structured songcraft and free‑form improvisation.",
